WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.031
hide some of those boxes from

00:00:02.165 --> 00:00:04.200
his own lawyers to prevent them

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:05.902
from fully complying with a

00:00:06.035 --> 00:00:07.870
federal subpoena.

00:00:08.004 --> 00:00:09.972
Here with me is the chairman of

00:00:10.106 --> 00:00:11.007
the house judiciary committee,

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:11.908
Jim Jordan.

00:00:12.041 --> 00:00:14.377
Thank you for joining me this

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:15.244
morning, sir.

00:00:15.378 --> 00:00:19.015
The indictment does say as I

00:00:19.148 --> 00:00:20.616
mentioned the documents included

00:00:21.017 --> 00:00:23.419
U.S. Defense, nuclear

00:00:23.553 --> 00:00:25.021
capabilities, potential U.S.

00:00:25.154 --> 00:00:26.089
Vulnerabilities to military

00:00:26.222 --> 00:00:26.422
attack.

00:00:26.556 --> 00:00:28.358
They were kept in unsecure areas

00:00:28.491 --> 00:00:31.094
like a bathroom, ballroom,

00:00:31.227 --> 00:00:31.427
bedroom.

00:00:31.561 --> 00:00:33.029
The indictment says Donald Trump

00:00:33.096 --> 00:00:34.630
lied to lawyers, his own

00:00:35.031 --> 00:00:37.033
lawyers, which resulted in false

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:39.769
statements to the FBI so he

00:00:39.902 --> 00:00:41.571
could keep those documents.

00:00:41.704 --> 00:00:46.209
Is any of that acceptable to

00:00:46.342 --> 00:00:46.476
you?

00:00:46.609 --> 00:00:48.144
&gt;&gt; Dana, the standard is clear.

00:00:48.277 --> 00:00:52.715
The standard is Navy virs Eagan

00:00:53.049 --> 00:00:53.449
a 1988 case, unanimous decision

00:00:53.583 --> 00:00:55.385
from the court that justice

00:00:55.518 --> 00:00:56.252
Blackman wrote the opinion and

00:00:56.386 --> 00:00:57.687
it said the president's ability

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.789
to classify and control access

00:00:59.922 --> 00:01:01.691
to national security information

00:01:01.824 --> 00:01:03.726
flows from the constitution.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:04.527
He decides.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:06.362
He alone decides.

00:01:06.496 --> 00:01:07.764
He said he declassified this

00:01:07.897 --> 00:01:08.131
material.

00:01:08.264 --> 00:01:09.732
He can put it wherever he wants

00:01:09.866 --> 00:01:11.234
and handle it however he wants.

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:12.402
That's the law.

00:01:12.535 --> 00:01:13.503
That's the standard.

00:01:13.636 --> 00:01:15.571
Jack Smith can do all this 37

00:01:15.705 --> 00:01:16.606
different counts or whatever he

00:01:16.739 --> 00:01:18.241
wants to do but that doesn't

00:01:18.374 --> 00:01:20.443
change the standard that the

00:01:20.576 --> 00:01:22.044
supreme court in a unanimous

00:01:22.178 --> 00:01:23.880
decision said was that.

00:01:24.013 --> 00:01:25.348
He can classify and he can

00:01:25.481 --> 00:01:26.115
control access.

00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:27.717
He has the sole authority.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:31.087
&gt;&gt; In this indictment he states

00:01:31.187 --> 00:01:32.622
on at least one occasion that he

00:01:32.755 --> 00:01:35.124
did not declassify the

00:01:35.258 --> 00:01:37.093
information when he is showing a

00:01:37.093 --> 00:01:39.095
document to somebody who doesn't

00:01:39.095 --> 00:01:40.096
have security clearance I might

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:40.363
add.

00:01:40.496 --> 00:01:44.233
He says, explicitly, it is

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:44.634
classified.

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:47.103
He didn't declassify it.

00:01:47.236 --> 00:01:49.472
&gt;&gt; Dana, he said time and time

00:01:49.605 --> 00:01:51.140
again he declassified all this

00:01:51.274 --> 00:01:51.507
material.

00:01:51.641 --> 00:01:53.376
This is the most political thing

00:01:53.509 --> 00:01:54.210
I have ever seen.

00:01:54.343 --> 00:01:55.878
They have been out to get --

00:01:56.012 --> 00:01:57.447
they are indicting president

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:58.781
trump on Tuesday for having

00:01:59.115 --> 00:02:00.516
material that he declassified

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:03.119
that was protected by the secret

00:02:03.119 --> 00:02:03.252
service.

00:02:03.386 --> 00:02:05.121
And the people who are doing it

00:02:05.121 --> 00:02:06.355
is the administration, the

00:02:06.489 --> 00:02:07.123
justice department from his

00:02:07.156 --> 00:02:09.125
opponent in the upcoming

00:02:09.125 --> 00:02:09.692
presidential election.

00:02:09.826 --> 00:02:11.461
I mean, this is as political as

00:02:11.594 --> 00:02:12.428
it gets.

00:02:12.562 --> 00:02:14.464
Frankly, Dana, it is part of a

00:02:14.597 --> 00:02:14.797
pattern.

00:02:15.131 --> 00:02:16.199
We have seen it time and time

00:02:16.332 --> 00:02:17.300
again with the president over

00:02:17.433 --> 00:02:18.468
the last seven years.

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:20.303
They try one thing then they try

00:02:20.436 --> 00:02:20.636
another.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:21.971
They've continued to go after

00:02:22.104 --> 00:02:22.305
him.

00:02:22.738 --> 00:02:23.940
I think anyone with common sense

00:02:24.073 --> 00:02:24.540
can see that.

00:02:24.674 --> 00:02:25.141
&gt;&gt; Okay.

00:02:25.141 --> 00:02:27.343
This is a very detailed

00:02:27.477 --> 00:02:27.743
indictment.

00:02:27.877 --> 00:02:28.778
A couple things you just said.

00:02:29.145 --> 00:02:31.547
Number one the secret service,

00:02:31.681 --> 00:02:33.649
they are charged with protecting

00:02:33.783 --> 00:02:34.317
the president.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:35.585
They didn't even know according

00:02:35.718 --> 00:02:37.153
to the indictment that the

00:02:37.153 --> 00:02:38.054
documents were there.

00:02:38.187 --> 00:02:39.589
So that wasn't their job.

00:02:39.722 --> 00:02:42.825
Number two, do you have evidence

00:02:43.159 --> 00:02:44.460
that the president, when he was

00:02:44.594 --> 00:02:46.362
president, now former president,

00:02:46.496 --> 00:02:47.997
actually declassified these

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:51.167
documents before he took them?

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:52.568
&gt;&gt; I go on the president's word.

00:02:52.702 --> 00:02:55.238
He said he did.

00:02:55.371 --> 00:02:56.372
The supreme court said that's

00:02:56.506 --> 00:02:57.173
what counts.

00:02:57.173 --> 00:02:59.175
We can have all the things jack

00:02:59.308 --> 00:03:00.776
Smith wants to say but everyone

00:03:01.177 --> 00:03:02.044
sees this for the political

00:03:02.178 --> 00:03:03.179
operation it is.

00:03:03.312 --> 00:03:05.181
The standard is the standard.

00:03:05.181 --> 00:03:06.048
I didn't set the standard.

00:03:06.182 --> 00:03:07.250
The constitution and the supreme

00:03:07.383 --> 00:03:07.817
court did.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.585
They did it in a unanimous

00:03:09.719 --> 00:03:11.187
fashion and it was an opinion

00:03:11.287 --> 00:03:12.522
written by justice Blackman.

00:03:12.655 --> 00:03:13.789
That is the standard.

00:03:13.923 --> 00:03:14.824
That's the fact.

00:03:15.191 --> 00:03:15.958
Jack Smith can write whatever he

00:03:16.092 --> 00:03:19.762
wants but this is so political.

00:03:19.896 --> 00:03:21.197
In 2016 -- I mean every election

00:03:21.197 --> 00:03:23.199
we've now seen this, Dana.

00:03:23.199 --> 00:03:25.201
2016 it was a dossier they used.

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:26.135
They knew it was false.

00:03:26.269 --> 00:03:28.271
They used it to go get a warrant

00:03:28.404 --> 00:03:29.705
to spy on his campaign.

00:03:29.839 --> 00:03:32.108
2018 the Mueller investigation.

00:03:32.241 --> 00:03:33.409
2020 they suppressed the Biden

00:03:33.543 --> 00:03:35.244
laptop story with the 51 former

00:03:35.378 --> 00:03:37.246
Intel officials.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:37.580
2022 --

00:03:37.713 --> 00:03:39.215
&gt;&gt; Let me stop you right there,

00:03:39.215 --> 00:03:39.348
sir.

00:03:39.348 --> 00:03:40.349
First I want to go back to one

00:03:40.483 --> 00:03:41.918
of the things that you said.

00:03:42.051 --> 00:03:43.486
&gt;&gt; Now they indicted him before

00:03:43.619 --> 00:03:45.221
the 2024 presidential race.

00:03:45.221 --> 00:03:48.057
&gt;&gt; On July 21st, a recording of

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:50.359
a conversation that he had said,

00:03:50.493 --> 00:03:51.727
quote, as president, I could

00:03:51.861 --> 00:03:53.229
have declassified it.

00:03:53.329 --> 00:03:54.764
Talking about a document he was

00:03:54.897 --> 00:03:55.231
holding.

00:03:55.298 --> 00:03:57.233
Now I can't.

00:03:57.233 --> 00:03:58.067
That means it wasn't

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:58.501
declassified.

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:00.403
But I want to move on to what's

00:04:00.536 --> 00:04:02.204
in this indictment.

00:04:02.338 --> 00:04:04.106
I'm sure you've seen the photos.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.608
&gt;&gt; Saying he could is not the

00:04:05.741 --> 00:04:07.243
same as saying he didn't.

00:04:07.243 --> 00:04:08.210
&gt;&gt; There are classified

00:04:08.344 --> 00:04:10.146
documents in the bathroom.

00:04:10.279 --> 00:04:12.682
In the ballroom stage, and

00:04:12.815 --> 00:04:13.983
classified information that

00:04:14.116 --> 00:04:15.918
he -- we're talking about

00:04:16.052 --> 00:04:17.386
information that the united

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.456
States shares with its allies,

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:21.257
critical information strewn on

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:21.891
the floor.

00:04:22.024 --> 00:04:25.895
Does that look secure to you?

00:04:26.028 --> 00:04:28.097
&gt;&gt; Again, Dana, the standard is

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:28.731
the standard.

00:04:28.864 --> 00:04:30.766
The president of the united

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.134
States can classify and he can

00:04:32.268 --> 00:04:34.270
control access to national

00:04:34.403 --> 00:04:35.871
security information however he

00:04:36.005 --> 00:04:36.172
wants.

00:04:36.305 --> 00:04:37.273
That's the standard.

00:04:37.406 --> 00:04:38.040
That's the constitution.

00:04:38.174 --> 00:04:40.042
That's what the court said in

00:04:40.176 --> 00:04:43.713
Navy vs. Eagan a 1988 case.

00:04:43.846 --> 00:04:44.447
I don't know how many more times

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:45.281
I can say it.

00:04:45.281 --> 00:04:46.449
If he wants to store material in

00:04:46.582 --> 00:04:48.517
a box in a bathroom, in a box on

00:04:48.651 --> 00:04:50.286
the stage, he can do that.

00:04:50.419 --> 00:04:52.121
That is just what the law and

00:04:52.254 --> 00:04:53.289
the standard is.

00:04:53.289 --> 00:04:54.123
&gt;&gt; That's not --

00:04:54.256 --> 00:04:55.658
&gt;&gt; Again, I think this

00:04:55.791 --> 00:04:56.559
underscores how political this

00:04:56.692 --> 00:04:58.260
whole thing is.

00:04:58.394 --> 00:04:59.729
Jack Smith -- you know how

00:04:59.862 --> 00:05:01.297
political it is when they

00:05:01.297 --> 00:05:02.465
selected jack Smith as special

00:05:02.598 --> 00:05:03.299
counsel?

00:05:03.299 --> 00:05:04.567
I actually sat in a deposition

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:05.301
with jack Smith.

00:05:05.434 --> 00:05:07.937
We deposed him on may 29th,

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.072
2014, because he was looking to

00:05:10.206 --> 00:05:11.707
prosecute people who were

00:05:11.841 --> 00:05:14.977
targeted by Obama's irs.

00:05:15.311 --> 00:05:17.313
People Lois Lerner was going

00:05:17.313 --> 00:05:17.446
after.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:18.347
&gt;&gt; Sir, you can keep talking

00:05:18.481 --> 00:05:18.848
about this.

00:05:18.981 --> 00:05:20.983
I want to talk about the

00:05:21.317 --> 00:05:22.652
substance of this indictment.

00:05:22.785 --> 00:05:24.387
I want to talk about the alleged

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:29.358
obstruction in the indictment.

00:05:29.492 --> 00:05:30.426
Here is what --

00:05:30.559 --> 00:05:31.827
&gt;&gt; You can't obstruct when there

00:05:31.961 --> 00:05:33.329
was not an underlying crime.

00:05:33.329 --> 00:05:35.498
&gt;&gt; Here is what the indictment

00:05:35.631 --> 00:05:36.298
said.

00:05:36.432 --> 00:05:37.700
Trump directed nauta, his

00:05:37.833 --> 00:05:40.770
personal aide, to move boxes

00:05:40.903 --> 00:05:44.273
before trump attorney one's June

00:05:44.407 --> 00:05:46.008
2nd review so many boxes were

00:05:46.142 --> 00:05:48.144
not searched and many documents

00:05:48.277 --> 00:05:50.346
responsive to the may 11

00:05:50.479 --> 00:05:51.580
subpoena could not be found and

00:05:51.714 --> 00:05:53.449
were in fact not found by trump

00:05:53.582 --> 00:05:54.583
attorney one.

00:05:54.717 --> 00:05:56.485
In plain English this alleges

00:05:56.619 --> 00:05:57.687
trump instructed his aide to

00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.021
help him remove sensitive

00:05:59.355 --> 00:06:00.389
documents in defiance of a

00:06:00.523 --> 00:06:01.824
federal subpoena.

00:06:01.957 --> 00:06:03.793
A, does that trouble you and, B,

00:06:03.926 --> 00:06:06.262
if he thought he had the right

00:06:06.395 --> 00:06:08.731
to have these documents, why was

00:06:08.864 --> 00:06:11.500
he trying so hard to hide them?

00:06:11.634 --> 00:06:13.402
&gt;&gt; No, it doesn't bother me

00:06:13.536 --> 00:06:15.371
because again you can't have

00:06:15.471 --> 00:06:16.072
obstruction of something when

00:06:16.205 --> 00:06:18.441
there was no underlying crime.

00:06:18.574 --> 00:06:19.675
The standard is set.

00:06:19.809 --> 00:06:21.410
The standard is what the

00:06:21.544 --> 00:06:22.678
constitution says.

00:06:22.812 --> 00:06:23.446
The commander-in-chief, the

00:06:23.579 --> 00:06:24.914
president of the United States,

00:06:25.047 --> 00:06:26.348
has the ability to classify and

00:06:26.482 --> 00:06:27.950
control access to information.

00:06:28.084 --> 00:06:29.018
That's what the constitution and

00:06:29.385 --> 00:06:31.053
the court have said.

00:06:31.387 --> 00:06:33.389
You can't obstruct -- you can't

00:06:33.389 --> 00:06:35.825
obstruct when there is no

00:06:35.958 --> 00:06:36.325
underlying crime.

00:06:36.459 --> 00:06:37.760
&gt;&gt; He is not the president of

00:06:37.893 --> 00:06:38.294
the United States.

00:06:38.427 --> 00:06:39.595
&gt;&gt; That is the fundamental flaw.

00:06:39.729 --> 00:06:41.397
When he was president he

00:06:41.397 --> 00:06:41.931
declassified the material.

00:06:42.064 --> 00:06:44.266
&gt;&gt; But he says point blank, on

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.001
tape as president I could have

00:06:46.135 --> 00:06:46.669
declassified it.

00:06:46.802 --> 00:06:48.204
Now I can't.

00:06:48.337 --> 00:06:51.407
He says in his own words it's on

00:06:51.507 --> 00:06:53.409
tape as part of this indictment

00:06:53.409 --> 00:06:56.078
that he did not declassify the

00:06:56.212 --> 00:06:56.445
material.

00:06:56.579 --> 00:06:57.813
Therefore, it is classified.

00:06:57.947 --> 00:07:00.683
&gt;&gt; Dana, saying he could have,

00:07:00.816 --> 00:07:02.118
saying he could have is not the

00:07:02.251 --> 00:07:03.519
same as saying he didn't.

00:07:03.652 --> 00:07:07.556
&gt;&gt; He said now I can't.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:08.824
&gt;&gt; Now he can't.

00:07:08.958 --> 00:07:09.425
Right.

00:07:09.425 --> 00:07:09.992
Because he is not president now

00:07:10.126 --> 00:07:11.927
but when he was president he did

00:07:12.061 --> 00:07:12.461
declassify it.

00:07:12.595 --> 00:07:13.062
He said that.

00:07:13.429 --> 00:07:14.296
&gt;&gt; Which means what he was

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:15.698
holding was classified.

00:07:15.831 --> 00:07:17.867
&gt;&gt; Not if he declassified it

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.101
when he was president of the

00:07:19.435 --> 00:07:20.770
United States for goodness'

00:07:20.903 --> 00:07:21.070
sake.

00:07:21.437 --> 00:07:22.338
&gt;&gt; He is saying point blank in

00:07:22.471 --> 00:07:24.473
this audio tape he did not

00:07:24.607 --> 00:07:24.974
declassify it.

00:07:25.107 --> 00:07:27.810
What you're saying just doesn't

00:07:27.943 --> 00:07:29.078
make sense on its face.

00:07:29.445 --> 00:07:31.847
&gt;&gt; Dana, what this truly is,

00:07:31.981 --> 00:07:33.449
Dana, is an affront to the rule

00:07:33.582 --> 00:07:33.916
of law.

00:07:34.049 --> 00:07:35.751
It is an affront to consistent

00:07:35.885 --> 00:07:37.820
application of the law.

00:07:37.953 --> 00:07:39.054
You have secretary Clinton who

00:07:39.455 --> 00:07:40.990
had classified material on a

00:07:41.123 --> 00:07:41.457
server.

00:07:41.457 --> 00:07:42.391
She was not president of the

00:07:42.525 --> 00:07:42.858
United States.

00:07:42.992 --> 00:07:44.093
She was secretary Clinton.

00:07:44.226 --> 00:07:45.494
You have that happen.

00:07:45.628 --> 00:07:46.428
Nothing happens to her.

00:07:46.562 --> 00:07:48.731
When you have two people who do

00:07:48.864 --> 00:07:50.399
the same thing and one has the

00:07:50.533 --> 00:07:51.700
standard that I've talked about

00:07:51.834 --> 00:07:53.469
but the only one who gets

00:07:53.469 --> 00:07:54.570
indicted is the Republican, the

00:07:54.703 --> 00:07:56.138
only one indicted is the one who

00:07:56.272 --> 00:07:57.473
was president and did it the

00:07:57.573 --> 00:07:57.807
right way.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:07:58.507
Oh, my goodness.

00:07:58.641 --> 00:07:59.809
That is what the American people

00:07:59.942 --> 00:08:00.075
see.

00:08:00.209 --> 00:08:01.043
The other thing that troubles me

00:08:01.477 --> 00:08:02.678
about this and this is total

00:08:02.812 --> 00:08:05.481
affront to the rule of law is

00:08:05.481 --> 00:08:09.485
that jack Smith went and got the

00:08:09.485 --> 00:08:10.920
president lawyers' notes.

00:08:11.053 --> 00:08:15.524
Talk about a violation --

00:08:15.658 --> 00:08:16.458
&gt;&gt; I want to go back to

00:08:16.592 --> 00:08:17.493
something you said.

00:08:17.493 --> 00:08:19.061
We were going back about the

00:08:19.495 --> 00:08:19.628
classified documents.

00:08:19.762 --> 00:08:20.763
There is something else I want

00:08:20.896 --> 00:08:22.498
to point out which is that the

00:08:22.631 --> 00:08:24.400
presidential records act says

00:08:24.533 --> 00:08:26.702
that upon the conclusion of a

00:08:26.836 --> 00:08:29.805
president's term in office that

00:08:29.939 --> 00:08:32.107
the president should not have --

00:08:32.241 --> 00:08:33.876
reading here, the archivist of

00:08:34.009 --> 00:08:35.511
the United States shall assume

00:08:35.511 --> 00:08:36.545
responsibility for the custody,

00:08:36.679 --> 00:08:38.614
control, and preservation of and

00:08:38.747 --> 00:08:39.748
